cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "shub-smale-tau9: Hardened Certification of z_max(9) = 6 and z_max(10) = 7 and Lean 4 Soundness Formalization for the Shub-Smale tau-Conjecture"
message: "If you use this software, Lean 4 formalization, or computational census, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "0xOsprey"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0xOsprey/shub-smale-tau9"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Shub-Smale tau-conjecture
  - Smale's 4th problem
  - straight-line programs
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Hardened exact-CRT exhaustive certification of z_max(9) = 6 over all of Z for
  constant-free straight-line programs, extending Santibanez-Leal (2026), with an
  independent naive Rust cross-check (tau <= 7), mutation suite, dual exact Z[x]
  verifiers (pure Python and python-flint), record witnesses up to tau = 18, and
  zero-sorry Lean 4.36.0 soundness proofs for canonicalization and per-leaf
  certificates. Developed with AI assistance (Antigravity Harness + Gemini 4 Neon).
